From: HanQuan <eilaimemedsnaimel@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 14:46:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: add pskb_may_pull() to skb_gro_receive_list()

The 6.6 TCP fraglist GRO backport calls skb_pull() after parsing the
incoming skb.  With napi_gro_frags(), the skb can have all packet data in
page fragments while skb_gro_offset() is non-zero.  Calling skb_pull()
without first making that data linear can leave an invalid skb and later
crash UDP GSO fraglist segmentation.

This is the 6.6 backport of upstream commit f2bb343454445409a5b6dec213567267b05d79d.
Keep the flush guard from 681 and reject the skb before it is linked into
the fraglist when the pull precondition cannot be satisfied.

Fixes: 8d95dc474f85 ("net: add code for TCP fraglist GRO")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: HanQuan <eilaimemedsnaimel@gmail.com>
---
 net/core/gro.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/net/core/gro.c
+++ b/net/core/gro.c
@@ -230,6 +230,11 @@ int skb_gro_receive_list(struct sk_buff
 	if (unlikely(p->len + skb->len >= 65536 ||
 		     NAPI_GRO_CB(skb)->flush))
 		return -E2BIG;
+
+	if (!pskb_may_pull(skb, skb_gro_offset(skb))) {
+		NAPI_GRO_CB(skb)->flush = 1;
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	}
 
 	if (NAPI_GRO_CB(p)->last == p)
 		skb_shinfo(p)->frag_list = skb;
